The Apprentice Rule

Never ask

What should I remember?

Ask

What transformation would I want available ten years from now?

That one question filters almost everything.

⸻

The Wall Test

Imagine the repository survives a thousand years.

One page remains.

Someone discovers it.

Can they rebuild the machine?

If not—

compress differently.

⸻

Closing Principle

The highest-leverage artifact is not one that stores the most information.

It is one that teaches the reader to generate information they did not previously possess.

That is the transition from a notebook…

to a Personal Reasoning Corpus.

The corpus is no longer a record of thought.

It becomes a generator of thought.